e outcomes), this definition does not apply — there are no favorable outcomes to compare. Therefore, the decision reason cannot be meaningfully applied to this decision problem because there are no positive outcomes. The skewness as defined is not operational in this context. Thus, the reason is not applicable to the problem.",
